    "interpretation": [
      "Near-field controls show that the direct component-kernel formulas and physical/metric transforms agree to floating summation noise.",
      "A and F^T use the scalar radial M2L path and retain approximation-sized far-field errors.",
      "Canonical F, expressed as D scalar-radial right-hand sides followed by a target-gradient diagonal contraction and the fixed external minus, retains approximation-sized far-field errors without introducing component kernels into M2L. Every row records and asserts a sign-sensitive unsigned/canonical witness.",
      "Wrapping gradient or Hessian components as scalar kernels fails under Ferreus reference-vector symmetry by six or more orders of magnitude and is disqualified.",
      "The frozen public interface has no target-Hessian output. The companion observed-hessian-windows-x86_64.json records a limited uniform-tree second-derivative fork; it does not change the public-interface fact or establish Auto eligibility.",
      "Hash-map/set traversal can change last-bit accumulation order between runs. These rows are the exact captured signed-probe run bound to the recorded source SHA-256."
